{"text": "Virtual reality sometimes shortened as VR immerses viewers in a simulated three dimensional environment. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Instead of watching a linear series of moving images on a separate and finite two dimensional screen, the VR viewer wears a special headset that makes it appear as if she is surrounded by a digitally animated environment or a space captured in 360 degrees by a specialized camera. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Like a movie, a VR experience can be curated by technicians and artists, they can provide us with engaging and spectacular things to look at. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> But virtual reality cannot control exactly when and how we see those things. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> For example, a movie can choose to show us a close up detail in a characters expression at a particular moment and in a precise way that conveys specific meaning and produces a particular emotional response. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> A viewer shown the same thing as part of a VR experience would not necessarily be close enough to see the detail and could even be looking the other way at something else at the moment that particular detail emerged.", "alignment": {"characters": ["V", "i", "r", "t", "u", "a", "l", " ", "r", "e", "a", "l", "i", "t", "y", " ", "s", "o", "m", "e", "t", "i", "m", "e", "s", " ", "s", "h", "o", "r", "t", "e", "n", "e", "d", " ", "a", "s", " ", "V", "R", " ", "i", "m", "m", "e", "r", "s", "e", "s", " ", "v", "i", "e", "w", "e", "r", "s", " ", "i", "n", " ", "a", " ", "s", "i", "m", "u", "l", "a", "t", "e", "d", " ", "t", "h", "r", "e", "e", " ", "d", "i", "m", "e", "n", "s", "i", "o", "n", "a", "l", " ", "e", "n", "v", "i", "r", "o", "n", "m", "e", "n", "t", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "I", "n", "s", "t", "e", "a", "d", " ", "o", "f", " ", "w", "a", "t", "c", "h", "i", "n", "g", " ", "a", " ", "l", "i", "n", "e", "a", "r", " ", "s", "e", "r", "i", "e", "s